      "body": "## Summary\n\n`BasePrefixCache.dec_lock_ref` declares `params: Optional[DecLockRefParams] = None`, but `UnifiedRadixCache`'s override (introduced in #36848) dropped the default, requiring `params` positionally.\n\n`schedule_policy.py`'s `_lock_node` calls `self.tree_cache.dec_lock_ref(last_node)` with no `params` whenever the acquire receipt's `to_dec_params()` returns `None`, even though `is_tree_cache()` is `True` for `UnifiedRadixCache`. This crashes with:\n\n```\nTypeError: UnifiedRadixCache.dec_lock_ref() missing 1 required positional argument: 'params'\n```\n\nRestoring the default on the override matches the abstract interface it implements (and every other concrete `dec_lock_ref` implementation, which all keep `params` optional) and fixes the crash. This is backend-agnostic — reproduced on Intel XPU across 17 accuracy runs, but the code path itself has no device-specific branching.\n\n## Test plan\n- Reproduced the crash on `lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.20-xpu` running `docvqa_val`/`gsm8k` accuracy evals for several models (e.g. `HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM2-2.2B-Instruct`, `CohereLabs/aya-vision-8b`).\n- With this one-line fix overlaid onto the same image, a 20-example `docvqa_val` run against `HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM2-2.2B-Instruct` completes successfully (exit 0, accuracy 0.4831, no crash).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36021321780](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36021321780)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36021321448](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36021321448)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36021322039](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36021322039)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
